<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed 24 civilians in Nigerian villages and bandits in Niger State murdered an immigration officer, burning his body, while bandits attacked Borgu LGA. A Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. The United States blacklisted Nigeria for recruiting child soldiers and Mali added 2,400 recruits, including 800 women, to its reserve force. Ex-militants in Akwa Ibom pledged support for President Tinubu's re-election. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTFBxMnl6YzNOYW9nQTRBbWVabTNHakhTMnJDQ0VyWFNyVnpRbXg3SG9HTWtQNFA3dDRqNUhNU2ZoY0FDSUtWVnVWVFoxdl91eV94NmtlZTBjelpjdG5ObE9RUDgzclFSMVk?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Spectator Australia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxNN2I5bUdHb29FVXdnQ2ZZQV8yOWpUUXJaQ1EwN1NYRVhud0hkY2FzTk14aG1SdmxkZUNkSFZLRXhMZ0wwc0t3MmRDeERHSE1XQUhWaVg2bnc3MWxSLVlQZkgwN2w1b1ZTRkJ5S09JbWhxbFJGUkU0VVdvUy1sVkxWNW96a0otWlJyaDE1V1BTbUxPeGdySFAxbFU3NHpZY3NyMFVzOUlZaDR2Zmk5eE9VcmFLcjI?oc=5&quot;&gt;Truth Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNdTFRSXdvaFN5X0R4Q0huQ24tLWZwWDBVbnRnQXhLVXRlUTZBVUpuYlIzd25uaFVtc1IzUDRGMjBJM0YxTDJfRGk1aUZEOUVjLVNZRGdDc1BXUWRvUlZ4OS1PRnQtZTRTNzFCc3NBV1N1Tk5GeE40Vy05RllCZWVDRE1ZbzZqZHN5SnVjczMwXy03LTg5X2x5d0UzeVBzcVJvRFd6RjlfMjRhQkU?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Eastleigh Voice&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxNSzcxdUhjQVpaalNqbHdVd1Vua0hHSDdaYkZoMFJGQVRiNFBQYlo1Ykdqdjc3TVRxUDBKMFEwYUF1RXhjd3NEdk9oQkJQMVRjUG1DbWtzc1JSWFN0bzVxTFBmZEo2aW1HX3pQN0VFUzNOUDhKZ1ZoZkg2ODkwd2tKRmdYY3BVSGVpWVFyZmZ2